  "full_response": "# Project Title\n\nA brief description of what your project does.\n\n## Introduction\n\nThis project is a demonstration of various methods to interact with APIs using cURL from the command line.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- cURL (version available on Linux, Mac, or Windows).\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use this project, navigate to the directories containing the code, then run specific cURL commands in your terminal.\n\n## Authentication Methods\n\nThe following examples demonstrate three different methods of providing authentication to an API through the `Authorization` header:\n1. Bearer Token\n2. API Key\n3. Basic Auth Credentials\n\n### 1. Bearer Token\n\nPass the Bearer Token as a header to authenticate or authorize one of your HTTP requests.\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN\" https://api.example.com/resource\n```\n\nReplaceYOUR_BEARER_TOKEN` with your actual Bearer Token.\n\n### 2. API Key\n\nPass the API Key as a header to authenticate your requests.\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY\" https://api.example.com/resource\n```\n\nReplace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual API Key.\n\n### 3. Basic Auth Credentials\n\nPass your username and password for basic authentication.\n\n```bash\ncurl -u username:password https://api.example.com/resource\n```\n\nReplace `username` and `password` with your actual credentials. For added security, consider using environment variables instead of placing your credentials in the command.\n\n## Advanced Usage\n\n- To include query parameters, you may need to pipe the cURL output to something like `jq` or include the query parameters directly in the URL.\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN\" \"https://api.example.com/resource?param=value&another_param=array\"\n```\n\n- If working with an API that requires a JSON payload for POST requests, include the `-d` or `--data` option:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_BEAR_TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"key1\":\"value1\",\"key2\":\"value2\"}' https://api.example.com/resource\n```\n\n- Use the `--compressed` option when communicating with APIs that require webp protocols compression to reduce the size of the response data.\n\n```bash\ncurl --compressed https://api.example.com/resource\n```\n\n## Contribution\n\nPull requests to the repository are welcome.\n\n",
